# Capacitor's own Android Gradle project generation (capacitor.settings.gradle, regenerated by
# `cap sync`) resolves plugin subprojects via relative paths straight into node_modules — and with
# pnpm's default `.pnpm` virtual store, those paths look like
# `node_modules/.pnpm/@capacitor+android@7.6.8_.../node_modules/@capacitor/android/capacitor`. The
# `+` (from pnpm encoding a scoped package's `/` for its store folder name) breaks Gradle's own
# dependency-graph resolution on Windows — confirmed live: `assembleDebug` failed with a bare
# `java.io.IOException: Invalid file path` while resolving `:app:compileDebugJavaWithJavac`'s
# dependencies, and ruled out both a space in the repo path and a space in JAVA_HOME as the cause
# first (same failure via a space-free subst'd drive letter and a short-path JAVA_HOME) before
# finding this. Hoisting puts real, flat copies of every dependency directly under this app's own
# node_modules/@scope/name — the exact shape Capacitor's generator already assumes — instead of
# pnpm's usual symlink-into-.pnpm-store scheme, scoped to just this one workspace package.
node-linker=hoisted
